This repository is the public pilot edition of a tax-document tracking app
built and owned by J Park & Associates. Its source is published so that the
firms testing it, and anyone reviewing it, can read exactly what the program
does to their clients' files. Publication is not a licence.

What this notice says

1. No licence is granted by the availability of this repository. Nothing here
   may be copied, modified, redistributed, sold, or used to run the app for
   any firm's clients except as the pilot terms below allow or as J Park &
   Associates agrees in writing.

2. Pilot firms use the app under the pilot terms shown inside the app at its
   first launch, which each tester reads, signs and accepts before the program
   opens (pilot/Tester Guide.md). Those terms govern the pilot; this notice
   does not replace them.

3. The app is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, for the pilot.
   The terms for firms that pay for the app are a separate document, prepared
   for the firm's attorney (pilot/DECISIONS.md, rows P163 to P166), and are
   not in this repository.

4. Reading the source, filing an issue, or proposing a change under
   CONTRIBUTING.md is welcome. A contribution that is accepted is accepted
   under these same terms: J Park & Associates may use and relicense it with
   the rest of the app, and the contributor keeps the copyright in their own
   work.

Third-party components keep their own licences

- The Python packages the app installs are named, pinned and hash-checked in
  requirements.lock, requirements-nodeps.lock, requirements-build.lock and
  requirements-gpu.lock; each is used under its own licence.
- The reader's models (RapidOCR's PP-OCR models on ONNX Runtime) ship inside
  the app under their own licences, which the packages that carry them state.
- The Electron shell's packages are named in app/package.json and
  app/package-lock.json, and Floating UI is vendored unedited under
  app/renderer/vendor/floating-ui/ with its MIT licence files beside it.
- NVIDIA's CUDA and cuDNN libraries, when the optional graphics card pack is
  built, are used under NVIDIA's licences and are never in this repository.

This file is a notice of ownership and of where the terms are, not the terms
themselves.
